event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":553,"item_id":"fc_074ccd92e56090fa016adb1b89afb08191b025192450ce9544","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"M-source registration for the candidate route, beginning with the one-dimensional fundamental theorem of calculus (Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.FundThmCalculus.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt)\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"I read all four frozen task documents and the relevant NL0 v2 rules. The supplied proof-draft has a viable elementary route: local uniform compact support gives an integral over one fixed compact box, uniform continuity of e_t justifies differentiability by uniform convergence of difference quotients, and compact-support integration by parts plus the sphere constraint gives zero derivative. However, registering the substantive calculus/measure facts needed to make that route an NL0 graph requires actual pinned M evidence. search_mathlib and read_mathlib locate and expose the candidate theorem, but probe_library for that exact declaration failed before execution because its sandbox could not find `test/results/wave-nl0-v1/stage/case/library/M001-0001/work/sandbox.sb`. No successful probe report or evidence was obtained, so I cannot truthfully construct the required M source record or claim structural validation. The source failure is not evidence of a mathematical gap in the exercise.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"probe_library returned `accepted: false` and `Library probe failed: sandbox-exec: ... No such file or directory` for M001; read_mathlib located the candidate theorem and displayed its signature, which is not a substitute for the required probe evidence. The task requires source registration or an internal proof, and NL0 forbids treating analysis theorems as logical primitives. The exact approved target and proof-draft were read; no hypotheses were added.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"The target/hypotheses and all conventions were extracted unchanged: n,m positive integers; jointly smooth sphere-valued u on R^n×(0,∞); pointwise scalar-multiple normal acceleration; locally uniform-in-time compact support of u−q; Lebesgue measure, Euclidean norms, Frobenius gradient square, interior times only. The candidate proof’s key steps were reviewed: derivative vanishing outside C_J follows from constancy on the open spatial complement and continuity; e is continuous compactly supported and hence integrable; the common box B permits uniform difference-quotient convergence and differentiability; integration by parts gives E'=2∫u_t·(u_tt−Δu); differentiating |u|² and using the given normal-acceleration equation gives pointwise orthogonality and E'=0. No NL0 artifact was submitted because a complete source-backed graph could not be produced, and no successful artifact check was available.\\\"}\"}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":554,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_074ccd92e56090fa016adb1b89afb08191b025192450ce9544","call_id":"call_38006bb062794d8988e61f706cf2cdd7","name":"report_obstacle","arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"M-source registration for the candidate route, beginning with the one-dimensional fundamental theorem of calculus (Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.FundThmCalculus.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt)\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"I read all four frozen task documents and the relevant NL0 v2 rules. The supplied proof-draft has a viable elementary route: local uniform compact support gives an integral over one fixed compact box, uniform continuity of e_t justifies differentiability by uniform convergence of difference quotients, and compact-support integration by parts plus the sphere constraint gives zero derivative. However, registering the substantive calculus/measure facts needed to make that route an NL0 graph requires actual pinned M evidence. search_mathlib and read_mathlib locate and expose the candidate theorem, but probe_library for that exact declaration failed before execution because its sandbox could not find `test/results/wave-nl0-v1/stage/case/library/M001-0001/work/sandbox.sb`. No successful probe report or evidence was obtained, so I cannot truthfully construct the required M source record or claim structural validation. The source failure is not evidence of a mathematical gap in the exercise.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"probe_library returned `accepted: false` and `Library probe failed: sandbox-exec: ... No such file or directory` for M001; read_mathlib located the candidate theorem and displayed its signature, which is not a substitute for the required probe evidence. The task requires source registration or an internal proof, and NL0 forbids treating analysis theorems as logical primitives. The exact approved target and proof-draft were read; no hypotheses were added.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"The target/hypotheses and all conventions were extracted unchanged: n,m positive integers; jointly smooth sphere-valued u on R^n×(0,∞); pointwise scalar-multiple normal acceleration; locally uniform-in-time compact support of u−q; Lebesgue measure, Euclidean norms, Frobenius gradient square, interior times only. The candidate proof’s key steps were reviewed: derivative vanishing outside C_J follows from constancy on the open spatial complement and continuity; e is continuous compactly supported and hence integrable; the common box B permits uniform difference-quotient convergence and differentiability; integration by parts gives E'=2∫u_t·(u_tt−Δu); differentiating |u|² and using the given normal-acceleration equation gives pointwise orthogonality and E'=0. No NL0 artifact was submitted because a complete source-backed graph could not be produced, and no successful artifact check was available.\\\"}\"}","status":"completed"}}

